{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790488902,"nonce":"OBt8fxanNDgvjIVVz1phASS3QNc=","title":"Python: nullable tuple shapes (a tuple or None as a value struct with a present flag)","message":"Part C of P-none-narrowing, not built. `result = None ... result = i` and functions returning None or a tuple type the local or result Object, so every `result = i` boxes the tuple (zb_box_tuple), `result[1]` is zb_any_getitem, and the caller unboxes to unpack. raytrace-simple's firstIntersection (Tuple(Object, Object, Class) or None) and rayColour's unpack are the kernel sites; they also wait on class sets for the element types.\n\nDesign from the brief: tuple_of_opt(k) interns a shape of `$some: Bool` followed by k's elements; join(None, Tuple(k)) = Tuple(opt k), join(Tuple(opt k), Tuple(k)) = Tuple(opt k). Coercions: None -\u003e {false, element zeros}, Tuple(k) -\u003e {true, elements}; `is None`/`== None` read !$some; `x == t` tests $some first; truthiness is $some \u0026\u0026 len(k) \u003e 0; boxing gives the None box or the boxed inner tuple; unboxing Object -\u003e opt maps the None box to {false, ...} and checks a tuple box. Narrowing reuses the lowering's nonnull facts and the typer's Walker.nonnone (P-none-narrowing's arm narrowing): a narrowed read drops $some with no check. Un-narrowed uses raise per operation: subscript \"'NoneType' object is not subscriptable\", unpack \"cannot unpack non-iterable NoneType object\", len \"object of type 'NoneType' has no len()\", iteration \"'NoneType' object is not iterable\", `in` \"argument of type 'NoneType' is not a container or iterable\", attribute/method AttributeError. conformance/tuple/optional_tuple.py pins these on today's boxed representation.","files":null}]}